// The keyframetracks package: property animation. Values that change over
// time as keyframes with easing, grouped into clips, played with cross-fades,
// layers and events, and built one-off with a fluent tween. A program
// reaches it with 'import keyframetracks'. It is Godot's AnimationPlayer and
// Tween, glTF's animation model and Manim's animation algebra, over
// geomath's values.
//
// The one invariant: **a track is a value as a pure function of time.**
// Nothing here steps a simulation. A Track, a Clip and a Tween's built Clip
// answer 'what is the value at t' for any t, in any order, forward or
// backward, so a clip can be scrubbed, seeked, run in reverse, evaluated at
// two times for a velocity, or sampled on a server and a client and agree. A
// Player holds the only state (its clocks, a fade, a queue) and its
// 'evaluate' is again a pure function of that state. Clips hold ids, not
// references: a binding is a target id and a property key, and a consumer
// reads a Sample (get a Vec3 for door 7's position) and applies it however
// it likes, so the package knows nothing of the scene, the renderer, the
// skeleton or the physics.
//
// - easing.cone     Penner's easing equations (quad, cubic, quart, quint,
//                   sine, expo, circ, back, elastic, bounce; in, out,
//                   in-out), smoothstep, CSS cubic-bezier easing solved by
//                   Newton with a bisection fallback, and closed-form damped
//                   harmonic (spring) motion
// - colorspace.cone linear sRGB <-> OKLab (Ottosson 2020), so a colour track
//                   can be mixed in perceptual or in linear light
// - track.cone      Track: keys with a time, a value (f32, Vec2, Vec3, Quat,
//                   Color, bool, integer, transform, vector of n) and an
//                   interpolation per key (step, linear + easing, bezier,
//                   Catmull-Rom, Hermite = glTF cubic spline); quaternions by
//                   exact slerp; trackFromGltf maps a glTF sampler on
// - sample.cone     Sample: the properties at one instant, with weighted
//                   blends and additive layers
// - clip.cone       Clip: tracks addressed by (target id, property key), a
//                   length, a loop mode (once, loop, ping-pong) and markers,
//                   with the exact rule for which markers a move crosses
// - player.cone     Player: play, pause, seek, scrub, rate, a queue, cross
//                   fades, additive layers, events
// - tween.cone      Tween: a fluent builder (sequence, alongside, lagged,
//                   delays, per-step easing) that builds a Clip; and
//                   clipSequence, clipGroup, clipLagged
// - codec.cone      a compact binary form for tracks and clips
//
// Conventions are geomath's: right-handed, f32, quaternions x y z w, colours
// linear sRGB. Times are seconds. Property keys are u32; the PROP_ constants
// below are the transform parts glTF animates, and the program's own keys
// should start at PROP_FIRST_USER.

mod keyframetracks;

import libc;
import collections use *;
import geomath use *;

// Property keys the glTF animation model names
pub const PROP_TRANSLATION = 1u32;
pub const PROP_ROTATION = 2u32;
pub const PROP_SCALE = 3u32;
pub const PROP_WEIGHTS = 4u32;
pub const PROP_TRANSFORM = 5u32;
pub const PROP_FIRST_USER = 1024u32;
